Z||000000||K9||09-06-99||03:46 PM||||I got riped off by Ed Kolson Pontic GM, in Surrey B.C.Canada. I have attached a copy of the leter that I sent to the owner.I have tolked the owner who stated that the would call me on the matter,two weeks ago,but never I never got a call.I don't now what els to do besides Kick someones ass... <p>Greag Barnes<br>General Manager<br>6280 120 Street<br>Surrey, B.C.<br>V3W 3M4<p><br>Dear Mr. Barnes,<p>Hi, my name is Arun Kumar and I am resent customer of Ed Klassen GM. I brought my 1985 Pontic Ferio GT for servicing on Aug.16/99 and was extremely disappointed on the service that bough I and my vehicle received. The following explains what happened.<p>I dropped my vehicle with none of the following damages to fix an erratic idle problem and check engine light. On Aug. 17/99 service advisor, David Hamilton, calls and says the problem is fixed and that vehicle is ready for pick-up. Total cost is $515.78 The following two parts were changed to fix the problem. The EGR solenoid and the EGR gasket.<p>When I arrived to Pick-up my car I found two new problems which were not there when I dropped my vehicle. The first one being the EGR pipe had a expanded crack in it. This crack was not there when I dropped the car. The Crack occurred during repair and should have been noticed by your employees. This crack created a vacuum leak within the engine which dose not help idle. The other problem found was the rear view mirror was not in it’s place but was sitting on the passengers seat. Your employees explanation was it “fell-off”.  <p>I was unable to get some one to fix the problem right away as per you service dept. The next day I went back to David and advised him of all the problems. Only after a long heated dissociation  your service dept. agreed to fix the two new problems that they created. I brought the car back on Aug.20/99 to fix the new problems at a cost of $200.<p>Well it’s been about a week and my car still has the same problem. I have spent about $700 for nothing and have gotten the run around from your staff including Mariam. I have tried to work this problem through Mariam but found her to be very mean. The only good experience I have had is Rosie calling me to see how the car is doing.<p>Thank you for taking the time out to read my letter and consider my problem. I am looking forward to hearing from you on this matter. I am shure if this was your vehicle, you would be just as upset. I have inclosed a copy of all work orders. You may contact me at...<p><br>
Z||000001||Patrick||09-06-99||04:41 PM||||<br>Welcome to the club. I was also screwed around by Eagle Ridge Pontiac in Coquitlam, BC.<p>A couple of years ago during a weak moment, I took the Fiero there to see if they could help get it to pass AirCare after I thought I had exhausted all possibilities myself. <b>Three hundred dollars later, the car ran like crap and failed AirCare with HIGHER emission readings!</b><p>I undid everything they screwed up to get the car to run properly. I then had the catalytic converter replaced. It passed AirCare with flying colors.<p>What was the Pontiac dealership's response to my complaints? Double-talk and bullsh*t.<p>I will NEVER go to a dealership again for servicing.<p><p>
Z||000002||Cooter||09-06-99||04:48 PM||||You should also call the regional GM headquarters and file a compliant with them. It hurts them because they like to be able to brag about satisfied customers in their advertising. If nothing else, a letter to your local newspaper gets a lot of attention. They will more than likely want to fix your problems if you make a lot of noise about it. My dad parked his Chevy 4x4 in front of the dealership with lemons all over it with a big sign saying "I got my Lemon at Buster Miles and so can you". It took a while, but they finally agreed to fix the truck and even refund the money he had spent having the faulty repairs done. I hate seeing people get taken like this.
