Z||000007||Punkndrublic||09-06-99||11:18 PM||||K9<p>Too bad I didn't tell people here before bout those guys. I took my car there for icbc repair when some noodle side-swiped my car back in october. I wasn't all too happy with their work or service. The paint is starting to rub off in areas where theres nothing rubbing it. They replaced the door skin with one from the reckers and never removed the old paint, which is red and is showing through my silver paint, which sucks. They never fixed my end link in my steering( thats where i got hit) and its now really bad, the door doesn't shut properly and is a little loose. Basically i come to the conclusion of F**k them and do the stuff myself, and get my dads friends to the hard stuff.  If you really need help, i joined the local fiero club and theres a couple of knowledgable guys, i think one owns a shop in langley. If your interested the website is<p> http://fiero.mainpage.net<p>We meet at the Pizza hut outside surrey place mall, every second saturday of the month. directions should be on the page
Z||000008||corbz||09-07-1999||09:00 PM||||I didnt realize there was so many BC boys here. I also took my car to Klassen and had less than pleased feelings about there "service". Also, my parents car (90 sunbird) engine blew a couple years ago. 3 months later and 2 seperate trips the job was done after originally been quoted for two. As for me they said I needed a new rack etc, two fix my steering. My personal mechanic looked at the car and said all I needed was a new gromet and an aligment. He replaced the gromets for $40 and saved me over $1000.||||reg||
Z||000009||Patrick||09-07-1999||10:50 PM||||<BR>Thanks for the offer Arun, but I don't want to hear any more depressing news about dealerships. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Yes, there seems to be a fair number of people from British Columbia participating in this forum. This could indicate any number of things:<P>A) There are a lot of Fieros in BC.<BR>B) There are a lot of Fieros in BC that don't run properly.<BR>C) There are a lot of Fiero owners in BC who are friendly.<BR>D) There are a lot of Fiero owners in BC who have no friends and this is their only social contact.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||
