Z||000017||Punkndrublic||09-09-1999||01:38 AM||||K9<P>this link works for me <A HREF="http://www.fiero.mainpage.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.mainpage.net/</A> <P>I cut and pasted it right out of the browser, As for your question, i don't quite understand, but anyways the next meeting is this saturday at 7:00pm in the parking lot of the pizza hut by surrey place mall, or at least thats what it was the last few times. I also live about 5 mins away  :-). Anyways i think we are up to 30 + members and we're only 5 or 6 months old, thats more then the performance ponitac club thats been around since the early 90's. You don't have to pay dues right now, and we re working on getting accounts with local parts stores and possibly a sponser. We just recently strip an 86 se down to the frame so there some cheap parts available too. There's a few diff fiero's, a choptop with an 8, some other guy that has an 8 mated to a stock auto tranny of all things.  One guy has two really nice near stock looking 87 gt's. And mines the most modified so far with bout 4 projects just sitting in my house collecting dust.||||reg||
Z||000018||Racer 1||09-09-1999||04:10 AM||||K9,<P>Sorry to hear about your bad experience. Can you take them to small claims court and try to get your money back?<P>My local dealership here is expensive but nice. I had a remanufactured pass rear caliper replaced for 300.00 but if I did it myself 99.00 for the caliper at autozone. I felt like kicking myself in the butt after that. <P>?? I think my Fiero has a poltergiest in it. Everytime I work on my geo metro my fiero brakes down the next day ??||||reg||
Z||000019||GWMORGAN||09-09-1999||07:56 AM||||I took my fiero (5 spd.) to a GM dealer in Katonah N.Y. for the cruise to be repaired (suddenly stopped working). I was quoted a price of over $250 (which I couldn't afford) for parts and labor.I eventually did the repairs myself which didn't cost me a penny. Turned out, the switch under the clutch pedal needed some adjustment to be seated properly. Most importantly,I picked up info from reading the threads on this forum and for that, I say a big thank you to you all for saving me over $250. THIS IS THE BEST SITE ON THE INTERNET!!!||||reg||
Z||000020||Cliff Pennock||09-09-1999||12:54 PM||||Racer 1,<P>I know what you mean - seems my Fiero has a will of its own too.<P>&lt;TWILIGHT ZONE&gt;<BR>As I see it, your Fiero does not accept <B>you</B> paying attention to any other car and will also not accept any one driving it besides yourself. My girlfriend drives my car once every two weeks or so, and when she does something <B>always</B> brakes down. And it's really never her fault. A few examples: radiator started leaking, waterpump broke, emergency brake cable snapped, rearview mirror dropped off, alternator died, turn signal died, fuel hose snapped (that was a scary one - it snapped in the engine compartment), car didn't start, and so on, and so on... Nothing ever happens when I'm driving it. And she driving much more carefully than I do. And the car really is in perfect condition so it has nothing to do with worn parts or anything.<BR>&lt;/TWILIGHT ZONE&gt;<BR>||||reg||
Z||000021||Racer 1||09-09-1999||05:20 PM||||Cliff,<P>WOW im surprised I thought my fiero was the only one doing that. About 5 years ago I let my best friend take his date to the movies in my 2.5 fiero. I drove his car out to my girlfriends house. Around 1:00 a.m. we traded cars at the local shoping center. My fiero started fine I drove for about 1/2 miles then all at once all the 3 bolts holding the UPPER alternator mount came off (ALL 3). Well you know what came next all lights died with the engine light on. Man im glad im not the only one.||||reg||
